From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kurt Fuchs <contact@fuchskurt.eu>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:04:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] coreboot: add locked-ro-store payload variant

Split the payload's variable store into two exclusive features:
spi-store (default, upstream behaviour) and locked-ro-store. The locked
variant reads a pre-provisioned EDK2 store from the RO_UEFI_VARS FMAP area
through the memory-mapped boot flash, reports it write-protected, and has
no SPI controller or flash-write code. The store's SHA-256 is fixed at build
time (CRABEFI_RO_VARSTORE_SHA256) and a mismatching region is refused.

Payload features tpm/xhci are separate; spi-store keeps both, the locked
variant leaves them out to minimise pre-boot attack surface.
